  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Capacity on Disaster Risk Management through Incident Command System in Timor-Leste</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM) and the United States Forest Service (USFS) aim to strengthen the capacity of the Government of Timor-Leste (GoTL) to establish an effective emergency management system that is used by all levels of government -national, municipality, and community - to enhance operations and coordination before, during, and after an emergency or crisis. Building on the gains of the previous engagement, this project completes the training of the cohort of Civil Protection Authority (CPA), municipal commanders, and first responders on Incident Command System (ICS). The graduates will become full-fledged local trainers and will be incorporated into the Civil Protection Training Centre for the sustainability and continuity of the project&apos;s efforts. ICS is a common language for coordination among entities for effective and efficient emergency management systems and is accepted and understood across the region, especially the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN). IOM, through logistical support to USFS, contributes to the priorities of the government on disaster risk management (DRM) and ASEAN ascension.</narrative>
  </description>
